{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAFdpgvLMB3wotygNqxV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The recovery middleware now handles a `panic(http.ErrAbortHandler)` the same way it handles a broken pipe. It logs a single line with no stack trace, skips writing a 500, records the error on the context and aborts. The change is in `recovery.go` and the related tests pass.\n\n**Not committed:** git has no user name or email set here, so the commit failed. The change is uncommitted on a new branch, `fix/recover-abort-handler`. Set your git identity and run `git commit -am \"fix(recover): suppress http.ErrAbortHandler in recover\"`.\n\n- **Test:** I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go`. It checks that the status code isn't overwritten and that no \"panic recovered\" stack trace is logged.\n- **Custom handler skipped:** a custom recovery function you pass in is no longer called for this panic, the same as for broken pipes.\n- **Not re-panicked:** the panic is swallowed rather than passed on to `net/http`. Because of that, the HTTP/1 connection won't be force-closed the way `net/http` normally closes it for this panic."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":34976,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":322,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25a2ff3a-4045-4434-a4c6-df1aaa4a5d35","uuid":"fd291f90-caa5-48ca-aa74-8e106c9f4786","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:27:13.908Z","request_id":"req_011CgAFdpUX8sSes4bhFNkRq"}
